===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[perform]] [[magic trick]]s.
#: ''He started '''conjuring''' at the age of 15, and is now a famous stage magician.''
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[summon]] (a [[devil]], etc.) using [[supernatural]] [[power]].
# {{lb|en|intransitive|archaic}} To [[practice]] [[black magic]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1971|author=Richard Carpenter|authorlink=Richard Carpenter (screenwriter)|title=Catweazle and the Magic Zodiac|publisher=Puffin Books|location=Harmondsworth|page=7|text="Thou great Norman lump!" he muttered. "If I '''conjure''' till Doomsday, I cannot make thee gold."}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|archaic}} To [[enchant]] or [[bewitch]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[evoke]]. {{rfex|en}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[imagine]] or [[picture]] in the [[mind]].
#* {{RQ:Landon Lady Anne Granard|page=51|volume=I|passage=There was a deep silence, while Helen's vivid fancy '''conjured''' up the scene. She knew the small neat room—she had been with Mrs. Palmer to see it; the cheerful garden filled with flowers, the hum of the distant play-ground, the rosy clusters of an acacia-tree, whose branches almost came in at the window;...}}
#: {{synonyms|en|envisage|imagine|picture|visualize}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|archaic}} To make an [[urgent]] [[request]] to; to [[appeal]] to or [[beseech]].
#* {{RQ:Addison Cato|4|2|passage=I '''conjure''' you, let him know, / Whate'er was done against him, Cato did it.}}
#* {{RQ:Melville Moby-Dick|text=Stammering out something, I knew not what, I rolled away from him against the wall, and then '''conjured''' him, whoever or whatever he might be, to keep quiet, and let me get up and light the lamp again.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|obsolete}} To [[conspire]] or [[plot]]. <!--a Latinism-->
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=2|passage=Drew after him the third part of Heaven's sons / '''Conjured''' against the Highest.}}

